IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pssca-offences`

-- Public Service (Service Commissions) Act 1956, ss 1A, 2-7 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_public-service-service-commissions-act-1956.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`a scholarship applicant who invents a degree on the PSC form` MEANS Statement WITH
    `connected with a public service application or a matter the Commission must act on` IS TRUE
    `given to the Commission, a member, or someone it appointed to assist it` IS TRUE
    `given wilfully` IS TRUE
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE

`a referee who wilfully overstates a candidate's results to the Commission's assessor` MEANS Statement WITH
    `connected with a public service application or a matter the Commission must act on` IS TRUE
    `given to the Commission, a member, or someone it appointed to assist it` IS TRUE
    `given wilfully` IS TRUE
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE

`an applicant who makes an honest mistake about a date` MEANS Statement WITH
    `connected with a public service application or a matter the Commission must act on` IS TRUE
    `given to the Commission, a member, or someone it appointed to assist it` IS TRUE
    `given wilfully` IS FALSE
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE

`an applicant who lies only to a private employer` MEANS Statement WITH
    `connected with a public service application or a matter the Commission must act on` IS FALSE
    `given to the Commission, a member, or someone it appointed to assist it` IS FALSE
    `given wilfully` IS TRUE
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE

`an applicant who wilfully gives a true but unflattering account` MEANS Statement WITH
    `connected with a public service application or a matter the Commission must act on` IS TRUE
    `given to the Commission, a member, or someone it appointed to assist it` IS TRUE
    `given wilfully` IS TRUE
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS FALSE

`a Commission secretary who knowingly tells a friend who got the scholarship` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `learned in the course of duties under a written law relating to the Commission` IS TRUE
    `made to an unauthorised person` IS TRUE
    `made in the course of duty` IS FALSE
    `with the President's written permission` IS FALSE
    `made knowingly` IS TRUE

`a member who forwards papers to a colleague as part of the work` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `learned in the course of duties under a written law relating to the Commission` IS TRUE
    `made to an unauthorised person` IS FALSE
    `made in the course of duty` IS TRUE
    `with the President's written permission` IS FALSE
    `made knowingly` IS TRUE

`a member who discloses with the President's written permission` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `learned in the course of duties under a written law relating to the Commission` IS TRUE
    `made to an unauthorised person` IS TRUE
    `made in the course of duty` IS FALSE
    `with the President's written permission` IS TRUE
    `made knowingly` IS TRUE

`an assessor who leaks by mistake, not knowingly` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `learned in the course of duties under a written law relating to the Commission` IS TRUE
    `made to an unauthorised person` IS TRUE
    `made in the course of duty` IS FALSE
    `with the President's written permission` IS FALSE
    `made knowingly` IS FALSE

`an assessor who knowingly tells an authorised officer, but outside any duty` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `learned in the course of duties under a written law relating to the Commission` IS TRUE
    `made to an unauthorised person` IS FALSE
    `made in the course of duty` IS FALSE
    `with the President's written permission` IS FALSE
    `made knowingly` IS TRUE

`a member who discloses something learned outside Commission duties` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `learned in the course of duties under a written law relating to the Commission` IS FALSE
    `made to an unauthorised person` IS TRUE
    `made in the course of duty` IS FALSE
    `with the President's written permission` IS FALSE
    `made knowingly` IS TRUE

`a blogger who posts a leaked interview report knowing it was leaked` MEANS Onward WITH
    `the information was disclosed in contravention of section 4` IS TRUE
    `the holder knew it had been so disclosed` IS TRUE
    `published or communicated it to another person` IS TRUE
    `for the purpose of a prosecution under this Act` IS FALSE

`a recipient who hands the leak to the police for a prosecution under this Act` MEANS Onward WITH
    `the information was disclosed in contravention of section 4` IS TRUE
    `the holder knew it had been so disclosed` IS TRUE
    `published or communicated it to another person` IS TRUE
    `for the purpose of a prosecution under this Act` IS TRUE

`a recipient who forwards the report not knowing it was leaked` MEANS Onward WITH
    `the information was disclosed in contravention of section 4` IS TRUE
    `the holder knew it had been so disclosed` IS FALSE
    `published or communicated it to another person` IS TRUE
    `for the purpose of a prosecution under this Act` IS FALSE

`a recipient who keeps the leaked report to themselves` MEANS Onward WITH
    `the information was disclosed in contravention of section 4` IS TRUE
    `the holder knew it had been so disclosed` IS TRUE
    `published or communicated it to another person` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of a prosecution under this Act` IS FALSE

`a parent who phones a PSC member to press for a son's scholarship` MEANS Approach WITH
    `influences or attempts to influence a decision of a Commission or a member` IS TRUE
    `in the course of the person's duty` IS FALSE
    `is a certificate or testimonial given to an applicant or candidate` IS FALSE

`an uncle who asks a friend to put in a word with a member, without success` MEANS Approach WITH
    `influences or attempts to influence a decision of a Commission or a member` IS TRUE
    `in the course of the person's duty` IS FALSE
    `is a certificate or testimonial given to an applicant or candidate` IS FALSE

`a teacher who writes a testimonial for a candidate` MEANS Approach WITH
    `influences or attempts to influence a decision of a Commission or a member` IS TRUE
    `in the course of the person's duty` IS FALSE
    `is a certificate or testimonial given to an applicant or candidate` IS TRUE

`a head of department who reports on an officer as the job requires` MEANS Approach WITH
    `influences or attempts to influence a decision of a Commission or a member` IS TRUE
    `in the course of the person's duty` IS TRUE
    `is a certificate or testimonial given to an applicant or candidate` IS FALSE

§ `s 1A`

#ASSERT `the body is a Commission` `the Public Service Commission`
#ASSERT `the body is a Commission` `the Judicial Service Commission`
#ASSERT `the body is a Commission` `the Legal Service Commission`
#ASSERT `the body is a Commission` `a personnel board under Article 110D of the Constitution`
#ASSERT `the body is a Commission` `a personnel board under Article 111I of the Constitution`
#ASSERT `the body is a Commission` `a personnel board under Article 111Q of the Constitution`
#ASSERT NOT `the body is a Commission` `a statutory board's own recruitment panel`

§ `s 2`

#ASSERT `the statement is an offence under section 2` `a scholarship applicant who invents a degree on the PSC form`
#ASSERT `the statement is an offence under section 2` `a referee who wilfully overstates a candidate's results to the Commission's assessor`
#ASSERT NOT `the statement is an offence under section 2` `an applicant who makes an honest mistake about a date`
#ASSERT NOT `the statement is an offence under section 2` `an applicant who lies only to a private employer`
#ASSERT NOT `the statement is an offence under section 2` `an applicant who wilfully gives a true but unflattering account`

§ `s 3`

#ASSERT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `between a Commission and the Government`
#ASSERT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `between a Commission and the President`
#ASSERT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `between a member and a Minister`
#ASSERT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `between a Commission and a head of a Government department`
#ASSERT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `between a Commission and a candidate`
#ASSERT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `between members in connection with the Commission's functions`
#ASSERT NOT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `between members on a private matter`
#ASSERT NOT `the communication is privileged under section 3` `between a candidate and a referee`

#ASSERT NOT `the communication may be produced in legal proceedings` `between a Commission and a candidate` FALSE
#ASSERT `the communication may be produced in legal proceedings` `between a Commission and a candidate` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the communication may be produced in legal proceedings` `between a member and a Minister` FALSE
#ASSERT `the communication may be produced in legal proceedings` `between a candidate and a referee` FALSE

§ `s 4(1)`

#ASSERT `the disclosure contravenes section 4(1)` `a Commission secretary who knowingly tells a friend who got the scholarship`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure contravenes section 4(1)` `a member who forwards papers to a colleague as part of the work`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure contravenes section 4(1)` `a member who discloses with the President's written permission`
#ASSERT `the disclosure contravenes section 4(1)` `an assessor who leaks by mistake, not knowingly`
#ASSERT `the disclosure contravenes section 4(1)` `an assessor who knowingly tells an authorised officer, but outside any duty`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure contravenes section 4(1)` `a member who discloses something learned outside Commission duties`

#ASSERT `the disclosure is an offence under section 4(1)` `a Commission secretary who knowingly tells a friend who got the scholarship`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure is an offence under section 4(1)` `a member who forwards papers to a colleague as part of the work`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure is an offence under section 4(1)` `a member who discloses with the President's written permission`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure is an offence under section 4(1)` `an assessor who leaks by mistake, not knowingly`
#ASSERT `the disclosure is an offence under section 4(1)` `an assessor who knowingly tells an authorised officer, but outside any duty`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure is an offence under section 4(1)` `a member who discloses something learned outside Commission duties`

§ `s 4(2)`

#ASSERT `the onward use is an offence under section 4(2)` `a blogger who posts a leaked interview report knowing it was leaked`
#ASSERT NOT `the onward use is an offence under section 4(2)` `a recipient who hands the leak to the police for a prosecution under this Act`
#ASSERT NOT `the onward use is an offence under section 4(2)` `a recipient who forwards the report not knowing it was leaked`
#ASSERT NOT `the onward use is an offence under section 4(2)` `a recipient who keeps the leaked report to themselves`

